The previous attempt had two problems. The `use` declaration sat at the top level of the WIT file, but it belongs inside the world body, and the `export!` error was a knock-on effect of that parse failure. I've also left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `LLMClient<inference>`, and adding an `http-client` import would expand its authority beyond that grant, which the body can't do. The fetch would also send untrusted message text to an external host. A change like that has to go through the graph's `with` declaration, not the node body. The output-unchanged requirement doesn't affect this, since the fetch would still leak the input.

